<main class="zd-faq-page">

  <section class="zd-faq-hero">
    <p class="zd-faq-eyebrow">FAQ</p>

    <h1>Questions before you support, join, or buy.</h1>

    <p>
      Clear answers about Ziyu Development, the apps, physical products,
      support, community, and the long-term mission.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="zd-faq-layout">

    <aside class="zd-faq-sidebar">
      <a href="#apps">Apps</a>
      <a href="#support">Support</a>
      <a href="#products">Products</a>
      <a href="#community">Community</a>
      <a href="#privacy">Privacy</a>
    </aside>

    <div class="zd-faq-list">

      <div id="apps" class="zd-faq-group">
        <p class="zd-faq-eyebrow">Apps</p>

        <button class="zd-faq-item" type="button">
          <span>What is Ziyu Development?</span>
          <strong>+</strong>
        </button>
        <div class="zd-faq-answer">
          <p>Ziyu Development is a founder-led ecosystem building apps, products, writing, and community around intentional living.</p>
        </div>

        <button class="zd-faq-item" type="button">
          <span>What apps are being built?</span>
          <strong>+</strong>
        </button>
        <div class="zd-faq-answer">
          <p>The main projects are Goal Grower, MyJourney, Blokkr, Kindlitt, and future experiments focused on focus, growth, reading, and better living.</p>
        </div>

        <button class="zd-faq-item" type="button">
          <span>Is Goal Grower available yet?</span>
          <strong>+</strong>
        </button>
        <div class="zd-faq-answer">
          <p>Goal Grower is currently in development. You can join the waitlist to receive updates and early access opportunities.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="support" class="zd-faq-group">
        <p class="zd-faq-eyebrow">Support</p>

        <button class="zd-faq-item" type="button">
          <span>What does “Support the Mission” mean?</span>
          <strong>+</strong>
        </button>
        <div class="zd-faq-answer">
          <p>It means helping fund the creation of apps, products, content, testing, hosting, and development work connected to the Ziyu Development ecosystem.</p>
        </div>

        <button class="zd-faq-item" type="button">
          <span>How can I support?</span>
          <strong>+</strong>
        </button>
        <div class="zd-faq-answer">
          <p>You can support by buying products, joining waitlists, sharing projects, joining the community, reading the journal, or supporting future donation/sponsorship options.</p>
        </div>

        <button class="zd-faq-item" type="button">
          <span>Is this a nonprofit?</span>
          <strong>+</strong>
        </button>
        <div class="zd-faq-answer">
          <p>No. Ziyu Development is a founder-led brand and development ecosystem, not a registered nonprofit.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="products" class="zd-faq-group">
        <p class="zd-faq-eyebrow">Products</p>

        <button class="zd-faq-item" type="button">
          <span>What products will the store sell?</span>
          <strong>+</strong>
        </button>
        <div class="zd-faq-answer">
          <p>The store can include journals, desk tools, books, apparel, accessories, digital products, and curated items connected to focus and intentional living.</p>
        </div>

        <button class="zd-faq-item" type="button">
          <span>Are the products random dropshipping items?</span>
          <strong>+</strong>
        </button>
        <div class="zd-faq-answer">
          <p>No. The store should feel curated. Products should support the mission and not feel like random ecommerce inventory.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="community" class="zd-faq-group">
        <p class="zd-faq-eyebrow">Community</p>

        <button class="zd-faq-item" type="button">
          <span>Can I beta test the apps?</span>
          <strong>+</strong>
        </button>
        <div class="zd-faq-answer">
          <p>Yes. Join the waitlists and community updates to hear about beta testing opportunities.</p>
        </div>

        <button class="zd-faq-item" type="button">
          <span>Can I give feedback?</span>
          <strong>+</strong>
        </button>
        <div class="zd-faq-answer">
          <p>Yes. Feedback is part of the build-in-public process and helps shape what gets built next.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="privacy" class="zd-faq-group">
        <p class="zd-faq-eyebrow">Privacy</p>

        <button class="zd-faq-item" type="button">
          <span>Will user data be respected?</span>
          <strong>+</strong>
        </button>
        <div class="zd-faq-answer">
          <p>Yes. The brand direction is built around technology that respects people. Privacy pages and app-specific policies should explain this clearly before launch.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>

  <section class="zd-faq-cta">
    <div>
      <p class="zd-faq-eyebrow">Still have questions?</p>
      <h2>Reach out or follow the build.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="zd-faq-actions">
      <a href="/pages/contact" class="zd-faq-btn zd-faq-btn--light">Contact</a>
      <a href="/pages/support" class="zd-faq-btn zd-faq-btn--light">Support the Mission</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "FAQ Page",
  "settings": [],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "FAQ Page"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}